{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"496617","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/496617","key":"MC-300558","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"02/Aug/25 7:13 AM","customfield_10050":"1459429","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<p>If you set the <tt>lock</tt> block data of a chest to an item predicate, the chest should only be openable while holding a matching item.  However, copper golems can open the chest whether or not the item theyʼre holding matches the predicate.</p>\n\n<p>This could be argued to be intended behavior (if the lock only applies to players), but it seems more consistent to have it apply to all entities that open chests.  It doesnʼt apply to hoppers, but hoppers arenʼt entities and cannot have items held in their hands.</p>\n\n<h2><a name=\"StepstoReproduce\"></a>Steps to Reproduce</h2>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li>Create a copper golem with a copper chest, and put a wooden chest nearby.</li>\n\t<li>Set the chestʼs <tt>lock</tt> NBT value to a predicate, for example {{\n{items: \"minecraft:trial_key\"}\n<p>}}</p></li>\n\t<li>(Optional) Verify lock mechanics for players: you can open the chest if and only if you have an item in your main hand that matches the predicate (in this example, a trial key).</li>\n\t<li>Put an item that does <b>not</b> match the predicate in the copper chest created in step 1</li>\n\t<li>Wait for the copper golem to attempt to put the item into the locked chest</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n<h2><a name=\"ExpectedResult\"></a>Expected Result</h2>\n\n<p>The golem cannot open the chest, or possibly never even attempts to use it</p>\n\n<h2><a name=\"Actualresult\"></a>Actual result</h2>\n\n<p>The golem opens the chest despite not having a matching key item.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":null,"customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/522772","id":"522772","filename":"CopperGolemLockDemo.mkv","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"},"displayName":"DHouck","active":true,"timeZone":"America/Los_Angeles","accountType":"customer"},"created":"05/Aug/25 12:37 PM","size":"32.06 MB","mimeType":"video/x-matroska","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/522772"},{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/522777","id":"522777","filename":"CopperGolemLockDemo-Downscaled.mkv","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"},"displayName":"DHouck","active":true,"timeZone":"America/Los_Angeles","accountType":"customer"},"created":"05/Aug/25 12:58 PM","size":"13.24 MB","mimeType":"video/x-matroska","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/522777"}],"versions":null,"resolutiondate":"29/Aug/25 5:16 AM","issuelinks":null,"updated":"29/Aug/25 5:16 AM","status":null},"fields":{"summary":"Copper golems can open locked chests without an appropriate key item","issuetype":{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net